# meta-deploy.list: the queue meta-deploy.bash runs, in this order.
#
# STANDING RULE (CLAUDE/AgentNotes.md): this list is exactly what needs running NOW. Add a
# run when it is pending, remove it once it has run and is done, leave out what cannot
# usefully run yet, then ask the owner to run meta-deploy.bash. Every step a run needs lives
# in the plan's own scripts, so this is the only command the owner is handed. The order is by
# dependency. A plan with none of triage.bash, deploy.bash and acceptance.bash has nothing
# for the script to do. A triage-only plan is run once, read-only. Words after the folder
# name are passed to that plan's triage.bash, both runs.
#
# One entry per line, three kinds:
#   <plan folder>                  its triage, deploy and acceptance scripts, in order
#   playbooks/<path>.yml           a change no plan owns; run as one unit through its own
#                                  shebang, which goes through run.bash, exactly as
#                                  ./playbooks/imports/<play>.yml does by hand
#   <plan folder>/<script>.bash    one plan script, for a step none of the three fixed names
#                                  fits; run as one unit, like a playbook entry
#
# A line starting with # is a comment and is the description of the entry below it: it is how
# the owner learns what a run will do, so write it. Blank lines are ignored. Any other line
# that is not an entry is a fatal error naming its line number.
# Plan 00194 Task 2.0h: installs the pingbus kit on the host and copies it into every declared
# LXC member's running container. `pingbus seat disconnected` (the host's notice for a session
# that ended without its goodbye) now writes each seat's outcome, told or why not, to the
# checkout's .claude/ccy/pingbus/disconnect.log. Before play-claude-yolo.yml.
playbooks/imports/play-agent-bus.yml
# Plan 00194 Task 2.0h: installs ccy 3.99.12.18, container 2.77.14: a closed terminal or tmux
# window now stops the session's still-running container before the disconnect notice, so the
# teams are told, and the clean-up ignores SIGHUP and Ctrl-C until done. The image carries the
# same pingbus, so it is rebuilt once at the next ccy launch. Running sessions are not touched.
# Before the 00194 acceptance.
playbooks/imports/play-claude-yolo.yml
# Plan 00194 Tasks 2.0b and 2.0h: the goodbye host checks, automated (acceptance.bash; the plan
# has no triage.bash or deploy.bash), run again for G3 (window closed). The last run passed G1
# (Ctrl-C) and G2 (podman stop) and failed G3: the team got no disconnected notice, because the
# launcher's exit ran while its container still held the seats (Task 2.0h, fixed by the two
# plays above). G3 now also keeps the launcher's stderr and the checkout's disconnect.log as
# evidence. The whole script runs again, so G1 and G2 are repeated. It makes two throwaway teams,
# starts three idle ccy sessions on them in a scratch checkout on its own tmux server, ends one
# with Ctrl-C, one with podman stop and one by closing its window, counts the goodbye and
# disconnected messages each team gets, then removes all of it. No SSH key or agent goes into
# the sessions. Each launch runs ccy's normal startup clean-up, which removes every exited or
# created ccy container on the host (as any ccy launch does). The team purge relies on sudo
# staying cached (it does on this host). One sudo prompt.
00194-agent-bus-live-delivery-supervisor-plugin
